lines=['# Fixed-basis GEMM-layout result','', '## Decision','', '**Equivalent layout qualified; application improved versus the old nested implementation; no complete-cost win over AngularBand.** This one bounded test is closed. No alternative packing, rank/eta/leaf change, mode expansion, physical RHS or GPU job was started. The six numerical comparison workers and bridge all completed.','', '## What changed and what did not','', 'The original space-major front is indexed G[i,a,j,b]. The new code computes Q*G on its left normal index with one 2D GEMM, packs the right normal index into the last dimension, uses a second 2D GEMM, and restores the original layout. Upward/downward Q operations also use a 2D GEMM. The exact identity is H[p,a,q,b] = sum_ij conj(Q[i,p]) G[i,a,j,b] Q[j,q]. All explicit packing and any implicit reshape copy are inside the measured operations. No expanded Q tensor I is stored. This is an execution change, not a lower-complexity algorithm.','', 'All previous basis-construction and attribution-control code bytes remain identical. The fixed basis fingerprint is `'+analysis['basis_sha256']+'`. Every measured nested worker independently rebuilds the same basis and pays its construction. The full scalar Q/B/D/U fingerprints, material/phase/directions/frequency fingerprints, Dhat and probes match. Basis ranks remain 8/13/16/17, eta remains 1.4091620147955772e-6, actual original derivative/directions and full 12-angle collision are unchanged.','', f'The inherited model defect bound remains {analysis["q_model"]:.12g}, with q^4={analysis["q4_model"]:.12g}. This is the previous exact-arithmetic error contract evaluated in ordinary floating point, not an interval-certified uniform floating inverse bound. The preconditioner is not the exact original inverse. Actual checks use original G, relative tolerance 1e-10 and at most 3 repairs, with no absolute floor for tiny RHS.','', '## Equivalence and accuracy','', f'The paid bridge checked all 14 actual nontrivial local transformations: maximum relative difference from the old einsum was {analysis["maximum_rotation_bridge_error"]}. Full raw factor actions on both the fixed single-column and five-column inputs also had maximum difference {analysis["maximum_raw_action_bridge_error"]}. This observed exact floating agreement is limited to these tensors/inputs, not a general bitwise theorem. The earlier small algebra unit also passed.','', f'All 36 checked comparison applications passed. Every method used exactly one original-G repair. Nested/packed maximum original residual was {max(r["max_original_residual"] for r in rows if r["method"]!="angular"):.12g}; AngularBand maximum was {max(r["max_original_residual"] for r in rows if r["method"]=="angular"):.12g}. Maximum accepted field difference from the original nested reference was {max(r["max_reference_difference"] for r in rows):.12g}. Exact zero and 1e-200 nonzero columns were preserved. No rejected numerical attempt or threshold rescue occurred.','', '## Actual cost, both rounds preserved','', 'All times below are milliseconds. Setup includes physical operator construction, candidate scalar nested basis and proof checks when applicable, V assembly and factor construction. It does not hide the basis or packing. AngularBand is not charged candidate-only basis work. Checked application includes all original-G residual computations and repairs; independent redundant acceptance QA is reported separately and included in the full process receipt.','', '| Run | Complete profiled setup | Factor | Rotation | Single calls 1/2/3 | Mixed calls 1/2/3 | Setup + all 6 checked calls |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---|---|---:|']
for r in rows:lines.append(f'| {r["label"]} | {ms(r["setup_wall_seconds"])} | {ms(r["factor_wall_seconds"])} | {ms(r["rotation_wall_seconds"])} | '+ '/'.join(ms(x) for x in r['single']['wall_seconds'])+' | '+ '/'.join(ms(x) for x in r['mixed']['wall_seconds'])+f' | {ms(r["profiled_workload_seconds"])} |')
lines += ['', 'The fixed order was original/packed/angular, then angular/packed/original. All workers were fresh processes with CPU0 affinity, one torch/BLAS/OpenMP thread and CUDA disabled. GPU was already occupied and was not used. The runtime records contain actual MKL/OpenMP team settings. No excluded warmup or extra repetitions were used. Each first call is retained. Single-column is the actual inner interface shape; the mixed batch is the previous zero + three random + tiny-column diagnostic, not a claim about batching physical RHS.','', '### Attribution conclusion','', f'Packed checked application means improved versus the old nested implementation by {(1-ratios["original"]["single"]["mean_wall_seconds"])*100:.1f}% for the single column and {(1-ratios["original"]["mixed"]["mean_wall_seconds"])*100:.1f}% for the mixed batch. The improvements occurred in both forward/reverse rounds. Raw-apply diagnostics also improved, but those diagnostics occur after the measured calls and are not substituted as end-to-end timings.','', f'Setup is not an established improvement: mean packed/original setup ratio is {ratios["original"]["setup_wall_seconds"]:.4f}, and the ranking reverses across rounds. Rotation totals for original were '+', '.join(ms(r['rotation_wall_seconds']) for r in rows if r['method']=='original')+' ms; packed were '+', '.join(ms(r['rotation_wall_seconds']) for r in rows if r['method']=='packed')+' ms. Thus the previous 64% wall fraction cannot be treated as eliminated compute. This run measured nearly equal CPU/wall in the factor phase, but did not profile dispatch/copy/BLAS subcosts sufficiently to assign the remaining difference to one cause.','', '### Strong-baseline decision','', f'Mean packed complete profiled setup was {ms(summary["packed"]["setup_wall_seconds"])} ms versus AngularBand {ms(summary["angular"]["setup_wall_seconds"])} ms, ratio {ratios["angular"]["setup_wall_seconds"]:.3f}. Mean setup plus all six checked calls was {ms(summary["packed"]["profiled_workload_seconds"])} ms versus {ms(summary["angular"]["profiled_workload_seconds"])} ms, ratio {ratios["angular"]["profiled_workload_seconds"]:.3f}. AngularBand wins this complete diagnostic workload in both rounds.', f'The single-application cold-start ledger also loses: mean setup plus first checked single-column call is {ms(summary["packed"]["single"]["setup_plus_first_seconds"])} ms packed versus {ms(summary["angular"]["single"]["setup_plus_first_seconds"])} ms AngularBand. Mean setup plus the three observed single-column calls is {ms(summary["packed"]["single"]["setup_plus_three_seconds"])} ms versus {ms(summary["angular"]["single"]["setup_plus_three_seconds"])} ms. These are accounting views of the same predeclared samples, not extra runs or a new workload chosen to claim success.','', f'The first-call effect must not be hidden: averaged over all three single-column calls, including the first, packed has ratio {ratios["angular"]["single"]["mean_wall_seconds"]:.3f} to AngularBand. But AngularBand pays a larger first checked call; the separately disclosed later-call means are {ms(summary["packed"]["single"]["later_mean_wall_seconds"])} ms packed versus {ms(summary["angular"]["single"]["later_mean_wall_seconds"])} ms angular. The mixed-call mean ratio is {ratios["angular"]["mixed"]["mean_wall_seconds"]:.3f}. No favorable first-call weighting is used to claim a faster complete solver.','', '## Memory','', '| Run | Persistent factor bytes | Factor phase highwater bytes | Application phase highwater bytes | External whole-process peak bytes |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for r in rows:lines.append(f'| {r["label"]} | {r["factor_bytes"]} | {r["memory"]["factor_phase_peak_RSS_bytes"]} | {r["memory"]["application_phase_peak_RSS_bytes"]} | {r["external"]["peak_bytes"]} |')
lines += ['', f'Persistent nested factors stay at {summary["packed"]["factor_bytes"]:,} bytes versus {summary["angular"]["factor_bytes"]:,} for AngularBand. The packing rewrite does not reduce this storage. Across all 14 rotations, the two explicit output-sized packs account for {analysis["explicit_rotation_pack_bytes_total"]:,} logical allocated bytes cumulatively, not simultaneous peak and not proved extra traffic versus the original einsum (which may also copy). Actual temporaries, scalar basis and operator/reference objects are included in process RSS.','', 'Phase highwaters are cumulative process RSS, not isolated allocation peaks. Packed has lower factor-phase highwater here, but the external whole-process peaks vary and the second packed process exceeds the angular processes. No overall process-peak memory win is claimed.','', '## Complete paid execution receipt','', '| Process | External wall s | External CPU s | Internal unpartitioned s |','|---|---:|---:|---:|',f'| bridge, including algebra QA and dual factors | {bridge_external["wall_seconds"]:.2f} | {bridge_external["CPU_seconds"]:.2f} | not separately partitioned |']
