lines += ['', f'Total numerical process wall is **{totalwall:.2f} s**, total measured external CPU is **{totalcpu:.2f} s**. These totals include Python/library startup, basis construction, checked and rejected work (none rejected), reference I/O, independent checks, diagnostics, allocation/GC and waiting inside the processes. They exclude development time and SSH/file-transfer overhead, which are not solver timings. The reference, all measured workers, plans and source copies were retained; raw CPU/wall times and all QA costs are in ANALYSIS.json. Unpartitioned time is retained, never subtracted from reported process totals.','', '## Stop and remaining scientific obstruction','', 'This bounded exact-layout experiment has produced a usable faster nested application path, but not a complete solver promotion. The setup gain reverses and strong AngularBand still has lower complete cost and cheaper later single-column actions. Scalar basis construction and the remaining hierarchical factor/action work cannot be declared free. No claim is made that this rules out all nested representations, larger problems, or shared-basis workloads. Such a change needs an actual workload/error/cost argument before expansion.','', 'Do not continue GEMM packing variants, rank tweaks or repeat-until-positive timings. Retain this equivalent implementation as the current nested attribution control if a substantively different mechanism is later justified. No next experiment was started or promised.','', 'For API semantics, the official PyTorch documentation notes reshape can return either a view or a copy and 2D matmul is matrix multiplication. Those are layout semantics only; timing and numerical evidence above come from the installed FWI runtime, not the current web-doc version: [reshape](https://docs.pytorch.org/docs/stable/generated/torch.reshape.html), [matmul](https://docs.pytorch.org/docs/stable/generated/torch.matmul.html).','', '## Reproduction','', 'Run bridge first, then run_worker.py with (original,original1),(packed,packed1),(angular,angular1),(angular,angular2),(packed,packed2),(original,original2), under the frozen one-thread CPU0/CUDA-disabled environment in LAYOUT_PLAN.md. Existing result directories intentionally abort rather than overwrite. The launch manifest, raw results and process receipts identify all source bytes. Production/E source hashes remained unchanged.','']
(P/'LAYOUT_REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines))
